  "location": "FAQ1 under MAR21.34 vs MAR21.33(1)",
  "text": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Basel Framework: FAQ1 under MAR21.34 vs MAR21.33(1)",
      "summary": "The FAQ to MAR21.34 uses 'at least 75%' for assigning an index CTP to a sector bucket while MAR21.33(1) requires 'more than 75%', so an index at exactly 75% maps differently.",
      "impact": "Position: Index CTP instrument, delta CS01 sensitivity 100; exactly 75% (by weight) of constituents are IG financials (bucket 3) Reading a: FAQ 'at least 75%': bucket 3, CTP RW 8.0% (Table 6), WS 8.0 Reading b: MAR21.33(1) 'more than 75%' not met; FAQ fallback bucket 16 'Other sector', RW 13.0%, WS 13.0 Difference: WS 5.0 per 100 of sensitivity",
      "correction": "Clarify or correct the cited passage so that the rule and its references give one result for the stated case."
    }
  },
